    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzsyjxxrsk2l",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "What happens to model performance on the popular DeepSWE coding benchmark if you make small alterations to the questions, like changing a file name to lowercase?\n\nModels that once looked very similar to each other no longer look so similar. maxxbench.unlap.ai/research/why...",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mzsyjxxrsk2l",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-08T18:00:45.577Z",
      "likes": 138,
      "replies": 9,
      "reposts": 16,
      "score": 7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.2,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 25.7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzqkydpmfd2h",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "I think there is too much concern expressed about verification of AI output in everyday work due to a risk of factual errors (there might be things to verify beyond errors, though)\n\nIt used to be true, but data on more recent models suggest they beat human experts in finding facts & checking claims.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mzqkydpmfd2h",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-07T18:52:55.793Z",
      "likes": 134,
      "replies": 18,
      "reposts": 15,
      "score": 6.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.3,
        "recency": 0.7,
        "age_hours": 48.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzltzpjm3k2c",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "I’m still kind of baffled by how surprised or even disbelieving some university admin are when I tell them that many (most? need more data) students are not all in on AI, actually…",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3mzltzpjm3k2c",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-05T21:51:26.703Z",
      "likes": 274,
      "replies": 7,
      "reposts": 58,
      "score": 6.4,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.5,
        "recency": 0.4,
        "age_hours": 93.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzvn2smcwk2h",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "I had early access to Fable 5.2 for a bit & I think  it crosses the line into being a sort of Jagged AGI. Here, I have it launch a business, do academic research, hack hardware, build 3D models & more. I think it is a good illustration of limits & powers: www.oneusefulthing.org/p/fable-52-a...",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mzvn2smcwk2h",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-09T19:13:24.698Z",
      "likes": 37,
      "replies": 0,
      "reposts": 7,
      "score": 6.3,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.7,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 0.5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzvki2l44c22",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "The corruption is what bothers me. In terms of the manipulation of the State for financial gain. And also in the use of the AI race narrative to restrict things (eg using export control against Anthropic) while simultaneously allowing NVIDIA to do something arguably more harmful to US interests",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mzvki2l44c22",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-09T18:27:08.011Z",
      "likes": 8,
      "replies": 0,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 1.3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:zlv6yt7cye6eihhy6cl5gl6g/app.bsky.feed.post/3mziv6j7pme2x",
      "handle": "garymarcus.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Gary Marcus",
      "text": "local-level midterm referendums restricted data center buildout (whether megawatt cap, zoning, outright ban, etc.) at nearly every opportunity.\n\nai oversight a top issue for incoming dem congress..",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/garymarcus.bsky.social/post/3mziv6j7pme2x",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-04T17:34:02.285Z",
      "likes": 50,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 12,
      "score": 4.5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.8,
        "recency": 0.3,
        "age_hours": 122.2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzisiq3hnc2w",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "I wonder if last night‘s US election results as they relate to AI will finally get through to the folks who have just haven’t been able to accept that not everyone is 100% on board?\n\nI do recognize that a lot of it is specifically data centers which are a narrow slice, but even so!￼",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3mzisiq3hnc2w",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-04T16:46:03.917Z",
      "likes": 28,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 3.9,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.5,
        "recency": 0.3,
        "age_hours": 123
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzjfistyyc2a",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "I do think that is part of it but I also think that some of it is just the very personal impact thing - like some people might not actually care much about AI but they don’t want a noisy annoying thing in their backyard.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3mzjfistyyc2a",
